# Environment files for React app
# Priority (highest to lowest):
# 1. .env.development.local (for local development - use this!)
# 2. .env.production.local (for production testing locally)
# 3. .env.development (committed to Git)
# 4. .env.production (committed to Git)

## For Local Development:
Use .env.development.local - connects to http://localhost:5000

## For Production (Render):
Use .env.production - connects to https://blockchain-certificate-verification-sj2j.onrender.com

## To switch:
- **Local work**: Keep .env.development.local (already created)
- **Test production locally**: Rename .env.development.local temporarily
- **Deploy to Render**: Uses .env.production automatically

## Current Setup:
✅ .env.production - Render backend
✅ .env.development.local - Local backend (localhost:5000)

The app automatically uses the right file based on npm start vs npm run build.
